{"ts": 1791259618.389833, "type": "step", "step": 21, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I won\u2019t paste the final writeup sentence for you, but here\u2019s the idea: pass^k means the agent has to succeed on every one of k independent runs/seeds, so it measures reliability. For your eval section, ask: if I ran my agent on 3 seeds, did it succeed on all 3? After you finish the paragraph, send me your draft and I\u2019ll help tighten it.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "pass_k"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: hm ok\n[activity] t=9 messages 2m", "t": 11, "activity": [{"t": 9, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.5759896480295166}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8084817897604412, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.39644044389342015, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
